E
crows cages cage~
   &+yA dozen crow's cages were suspended from trees before the area was
cleared, long ago, forming an open space at the center.
&+yThis was how it stood, presumably, before two of the trees have fallen,
with another one leaning dramatically and ready to collapse as well.
&+yOne of the other cages supportive branches was sawed off with an even cut,
leaving a total of three cages strewn upon the ground, consumed by
overgrowth. One of the two cages on the northeastern corner of the clearing
&+yis missing its door and has been enveloped by a massive oak tree,
having literally grown around the metal. This leaves eight operable cages,
&+ysix on the southern, shaded perimeter of the clearing and two adjacent
to the northern path, fully operable and as far as one may assume - still
&+yused for the prolonged executions of thieves and outcasts in a cruel display.
~
